Gardenfell: where its parts come from

Gardenfell is Robin Hjelte's. The engine crates under crates/ and the command line are
MIT (see LICENSE and each crate's own LICENSE). The page under page-source/ is built from
parts, each saying at its top which licence it carries: MIT for Robin's own, GPL-2.0 for
the seven renderer parts that carry code ported from MGE XE, which is GPL-2.0; the built
Gardenfell.html and ui/index.html contain them all and are GPL-2.0 as a whole. This file
names every piece that was taken from somewhere else or written to match something
else's behaviour, so that nobody has to read the source to find out.

What the engine grew from:

  crates/                     the scattering and the engine side began from
                              grass-experiments, Greatness7's Rust project, with
                              wazabear and herbert, who helped on it. Shared with Robin
                              under free permission ("Sure, free perms. It was planned to
                              be MIT license if we ever got it releasable. Give credit to
                              wazabear and herbert since they helped on it."); the
                              collision semantics of the placement pass and the shape of
                              the scatter are its, rewritten here as Gardenfell's own MIT
                              code.

Code ported into the page (GPL-2.0, MGE XE, https://github.com/Hrnchamd/MGE-XE, with
the fork by G7 that Robin runs):

  page-source/06_mge.js       what the renderer (06_gl.js, MIT) took from MGE XE, kept
                              in one file and interpolated into its shaders: the grass
                              wind (XE Mod Grass.fx, grassDisplacement), the grass cutout
                              and wrap lighting, the static tonemap of XE FixedFuncEmu.fx,
                              XE Common.fx's fogColourScatter, fogColour and fogColourSky
                              with the sun-altitude terms, the shadow receiver of XE Mod
                              Shadow.fx with its core-mod constants verbatim, and the
                              point-light decode of ffeshader.cpp
  page-source/26_water.js     XE Mod Water.fx and Sunshafts.fx
  page-source/29_ssao.js      SSAO HQ.fx, based on ssao v09 by Knu, as distributed with
                              MGE XE; used with the author's permission, given to Robin:
                              "Totally OK to use code in the shader"
  page-source/35_underwater.js  the under-water effects and XE Mod Caustics.fx
  page-source/36_dof.js       Depth of Field.fx (v12 by Knu, tweaked by peachykeen)
  page-source/37_shadow.js    rendershadow.cpp: the cascades, their placement and the
                              caster rules, at MGE XE's numbers

Code ported into the page under its own notice:

  page-source/33_fxaa.js      FXAA 3.11 by Timothy Lottes, NVIDIA, under NVIDIA's notice,
                              which the file carries; the MGE XE port is J. Böttcher's,
